((date 2026-09-14) (slug concentration-deploy-probe)
 (hypothesis
  "Item 3 of the 09-14 queue / item 6 of the 09-13 queue: the record's entry-side gap is a DEPLOYMENT problem - in a recovery the screener admits 20 names a week (long_top_n_admitted = 20 on every screening week through spring 2020 in the 2019 grid null) but the book fills 1-3, so raising per-position size (c1: max_position_pct_long 0.14 -> 0.25) or the aggregate deployment (c2: max_long_exposure_pct 0.70 -> 0.85 with min_cash_pct 0.30 -> 0.15) should capture more of the recovery. Prior: project_capacity_concentration_surface (06-25, sp500 single path): concentration is a return-for-drawdown trade-off with a knife-edge at 0.25; exposure alone inert.")
 (base_scenario
  "concentration-deploy-2026-09-13: arms c1-conc25 / c2-deploy85 = the a0-breadth-on-null spec with one portfolio_config value replaced in place, on the 26y top-3000 PIT-2000 _v10dedup record (build main 90552b910, pinned worktree sweep-conc), salts 0/1/2, paired against the committed a0-breadth-on-null-s{0,1,2}-v10 nulls (build 969637974; runtime-inert delta by inspection). Pairing gate validator_diff -check V6 exit 0 on every pair read (V6 = 0). Pre-registered (PR #2796, before any cell ran): an arm clears if realised P&L AND Calmar beat the null at >= 2 of 3 salts; level not a criterion; the Recovering-week cohort's paired P&L is the item-6 number. c2 was stopped by the dispatcher after salt 0 (bit-identical to the null); All c1 salts complete (lane done 02:29 PT 09-14): salt 2 realised $2.70M -> $1.74M (-$963k), Calmar 0.183 -> 0.094, maxDD flat (43.0 -> 42.7; the null is its open-MTM cell) - 3 of 3 fail.")
 (window_id top3000-2000-2026-record-26y-3salt) (baseline_label record-breadth-on-null-v10dedup)
 (variants
  (
   ((label null-a0-v10dedup-s0) (config_hash null-record-convention)
    (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.4453) (mean_calmar 0.1629) (mean_return_pct 382.74) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 37.60)))))
   ((label c1-conc25-s0) (config_hash max_position_pct_long-0.25)
    (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.4031) (mean_calmar 0.1590) (mean_return_pct 313.12) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 34.61)))))
   ((label c2-deploy85-s0) (config_hash exposure-0.85-cash-0.15)
    (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.4453) (mean_calmar 0.1629) (mean_return_pct 382.74) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 37.60)))))
   ((label null-a0-v10dedup-s1) (config_hash null-record-convention)
    (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.4272) (mean_calmar 0.1676) (mean_return_pct 311.75) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 32.75)))))
   ((label c1-conc25-s1) (config_hash max_position_pct_long-0.25)
    (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.3368) (mean_calmar 0.0918) (mean_return_pct 204.08) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 46.74)))))
   ((label null-a0-v10dedup-s2) (config_hash null-record-convention)
    (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.5260) (mean_calmar 0.1827) (mean_return_pct 639.74) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 42.96)))))
   ((label c1-conc25-s2) (config_hash max_position_pct_long-0.25)
    (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.3179) (mean_calmar 0.0942) (mean_return_pct 184.29) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 42.71)))))
  ))
 (verdict Reject)
 (notes
  "NEITHER ARM CLEARS; the deploy-more-in-recoveries hypothesis has no lever on this base. c2-deploy85 is INERT: trades.csv identical row for row and every metric identical to the null at salt 0 (382.74 / 710 / 0.445 / 37.60) while params.sexp confirms the overrides took - at 0.14 per position the book never reaches the 70% ceiling or the 30% cash floor (max nine concurrent names, risk-based sizing below the cap), reproducing the 06-25 exposure-inert finding on the broad record and extending it to the cash floor. c1-conc25 FAILS both criteria at all three salts: s0 realised $3.24M -> $2.82M (-$421k), Calmar 0.163 -> 0.159, maxDD 37.6 -> 34.6; s1 realised $2.94M -> $2.05M (-$892k), Calmar 0.168 -> 0.092, maxDD 32.8 -> 46.7 (episode 2017-10 -> 2020-06). WHY (transferable): the shared-trade term is positive at both salts (+$574k / +$311k - the same trades earn more at the wider cap) but concentration cuts the trade count by a third (710 -> 474, 707 -> 504) and the concurrent-name count (4-6 vs 5-9 in 2020), so the book is fuller per name and emptier per slot exactly when the recovery monsters screen in: NVDA 2020-04-06 and BBWI 2020-08-08 are null-only at both salts and the arm's 2020 realised falls from +$1.69M / +$1.10M to +$0.89M / -$0.17M. The Recovering-week cohort (the item-6 number) is 11-20 trades - far below the 230-trade floor - and its sign is a draw: +$122k at s0 (n=18 -> 11, mean +$28k -> +$56k), -$402k at s1 (n=20 -> 16). The drawdown side is unambiguous: a concentrated book rides 2018 and 2020 deeper. This is the 06-25 'knife-edge at 0.25' reproduced with salts: the 0.25 cell is a lottery. Same law as project_edge_is_the_fat_tail from the other side - a bigger ticket in fewer names buys less breadth in the weeks the tail is caught. CONSEQUENCES: item 6 (Recovering-week deployment ramp) = NO-BUILD; max_long_exposure_pct / min_cash_pct can be dropped from capacity surfaces on this base (inert); max_position_pct_long stays an axis with a documented REJECT-as-default at 0.25 (keep 0.14 on the record). The entry-side gap remains top-of-funnel (breakout gate + top-N, project_monster_funnel_top_of_funnel), not funding or sizing. Artifacts: concentration-deploy-2026-09-13/results/{c1-conc25-s0,c1-conc25-s1,c2-deploy85-s0}-v10-* incl. equity_curve.csv, paired against stop-width-by-state-2026-09-08/results/a0-breadth-on-null-s{0,1}-v10-*. Related ledger: 2026-09-13-stop-width-12pct-weekly-confirmation-grid (the same session's other regime-dependence reversal), 2026-06-25 capacity concentration surface."))
